**Most severe real defects:**

A. **Auth hint regression** (mcpCommand.ts ~line 263): disconnected auth-needed server no longer shows `/mcp auth` hint when both tools and prompts are empty. Real wrong-result/UX regression.

B. **Empty-string argument drop** (promptCommands.ts, `if (value)`): passing `--arg=""` is treated as missing; required arg errors, optional dropped. Real wrong-result bug.

C. **Prompt name collision across servers** (promptCommands.ts `commandName = prompt.name`): two servers with same prompt name → one command silently overrides. Real bug.

D. **`discoverTools` throw removal** (mcp-client.ts): removed `if (discoveredTools.length === 0) throw`. Behavior contract change; a server with no enabled tools now silently succeeds. Defensive check removed.

E. **Pagination ignored in `prompts/list`** (mcp-client.ts discoverPrompts): only first page of prompts; servers with >200 prompts (SDK page size) silently drop the rest. Real wrong-result under pagination.

F. **invokeMcpPrompt logs `promptParams`** (mcp-client.ts): sensitive argument values logged to console. Privacy/security minor.

G. **Stale prompt cache / command set never refreshes** (promptCommands.ts + mcp-client.ts): `createPromptCommands` reads cache once; reconnects with changed prompts not reflected. Design concern.

H. **Completion produces malformed suggestions** (promptCommands.ts completion): `${partialArg}--${arg.name}=""` without space separator → `--ke--other=""`; also no trailing handling.

I. **Command kind/name**: slash commands named after raw prompt names — could contain characters invalid for slash command parsing (spaces, slashes in prompt names). A prompt named "my prompt" or with a slash would create a broken command. Real edge.

J. **`mcpServerPromptsInternal` leak**: no cleanup when server removed cleanly (only on onerror). Minor.

Let me also reconsider the `JSON.stringify(result.messages[0].content.text)` — the submit_prompt content. If text contains newlines/quotes, this produces a JSON-escaped string with wrapping quotes which may display oddly. Uncertain — I'll mention as low.

